IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Pennsylvania Human Services Code (Act of Jun. 13, 1967, P.L. 31, No. 21; formerly the Public Welfare Code), Article IV,
-- Public Assistance -- the seat-neutral core, in the Article's own terms, for cash assistance:
--   the classes of needy persons eligible (s 432(1)-(3)) and the end of general assistance cash (s 403.2(a));
--   the conditions that bar assistance (s 432(4), (5)(i), (9), (10); s 432.22) and the strike month (s 432(6));
--   resources (s 432.5(b), (c)); whose income counts and the earned income disregard (s 432.12(a));
--   the cap for a family resident less than twelve months (s 432(5)(ii));
--   the RESET work requirements and their exemptions (s 405.1(a.2)-(a.4)) and the disqualification for failing them (s 432.3);
--   reporting changes (s 432.14(b)), timely notice (s 432.17) and assistance pending a fair hearing (s 423(a)).
-- Duties with a deadline are regulative rules; amounts and tests are functions.
--
-- "Aid to families with dependent children" is the Code's name for the cash assistance Pennsylvania now pays with federal
-- TANF funds (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq., deposited at us/social-security-act); the Code has not been re-worded.
--
-- Edition: the whole Act as served by the Pennsylvania General Assembly (palegis.us) on 24 October 2026, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/pa-1967-act-21-human-services-code.txt; Article IV is at lines 1299-5284.
-- The payment standards (the family size allowances) are set by department regulation (55 Pa. Code ch. 175), not in the
-- Code, and are not deposited: the amount of a grant is not computed here.
--
-- The seat questions are in pa-hsc-seat.l4. BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Services Code, Article IV -- Public Assistance (cash assistance)`

§§ `s 432(1)-(3), s 403.2 -- the classes of needy persons eligible`

-- s 432: "needy persons of the classes defined in clauses (1), (2), and (3) shall be eligible for assistance: (1) Persons
-- for whose assistance Federal financial participation is available to the Commonwealth as aid to families with dependent
-- children or as other assistance, and which assistance is not precluded by other provisions of law." Whether federal
-- financial participation is available (the federal TANF tests: a child, a caretaker relative, the 60-month limit of
-- 42 U.S.C. 608(a)(7)) is a borrowed test, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `federal financial participation is available for my family's assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is of the class eligible for aid to families with dependent children` IF
    `federal financial participation is available for my family's assistance`

-- s 432(2)(i): "State supplemental assistance shall be granted to persons who receive Federal supplemental security
-- income for the aged, blind and disabled pursuant to Title XVI". (ii): "shall also be granted to persons who are aged,
-- blind and disabled, as defined in Title XVI ..., and whose income, pursuant to the standards and income disregards of
-- Title XVI ..., is less than the combined income of the Federal payments under the supplemental security income program
-- and the State supplemental assistance payments". The combined amount is set by the department (s 432(2)(iii)); input.
GIVEN `receives federal supplemental security income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is aged, blind or disabled as defined in Title XVI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `income counted under the Title XVI standards and disregards` IS A NUMBER
      `the combined federal SSI payment and State supplemental assistance payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for State supplemental assistance` IF
        `receives federal supplemental security income`
    OR  (    `is aged, blind or disabled as defined in Title XVI`
         AND `income counted under the Title XVI standards and disregards` LESS THAN `the combined federal SSI payment and State supplemental assistance payment`)

-- s 432(3) still lists the classes eligible for general assistance, but s 403.2(a): "notwithstanding any other provision
-- of law, the general assistance cash assistance program shall cease August 1, 2019." (b): general assistance-related
-- medical assistance continues.
DECLARE `General assistance cash` IS ONE OF
    `no general assistance cash is payable: the program ceased on August 1, 2019 (s 403.2(a)); general assistance-related medical assistance continues (s 403.2(b))`
    `general assistance cash could be payable for this day, which is before August 1, 2019, if the person was in a class of s 432(3)`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `General assistance cash`
`general assistance cash on` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2019)
    THEN `no general assistance cash is payable: the program ceased on August 1, 2019 (s 403.2(a)); general assistance-related medical assistance continues (s 403.2(b))`
    ELSE `general assistance cash could be payable for this day, which is before August 1, 2019, if the person was in a class of s 432(3)`

§§ `s 432(4), (5)(i), (9), (10), s 432.22 -- what bars assistance`

DECLARE `Bar to assistance` IS ONE OF
    `not a citizen, and federal law does not specifically require assistance (s 432.22)`
    `not a resident of Pennsylvania (s 432(5)(i)); a transient may be given up to seven days of assistance as vendor payments`
    `an inmate of a public institution (s 432(4)(ii))`
    `disposed of property worth $500 or more without fair consideration in the two years before applying, and not eligible for State supplemental assistance (s 432(4)(i))`
    `sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor and has not satisfied the penalty (s 432(9))`
    `an unmarried parent under 18 who is not living with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative or in an approved adult-supervised arrangement, and no exception applies (s 432(10))`

-- s 432(9): "Assistance may not be granted to any person who has been sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor offense and
-- who has not otherwise satisfied the penalty ... 'satisfied the penalty' means completed the period of incarceration or
-- extension thereof and paid all fines, costs and restitution. Nothing in this clause shall be deemed to exclude from cash
-- assistance any person who has been paroled from a term of imprisonment, or any person who is in compliance with all
-- terms of probation, and who has made either full payment of all fines, costs and restitution or is in compliance with an
-- approved payment plan."
GIVEN `sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `completed the period of incarceration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid all fines, costs and restitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paroled, or in compliance with all terms of probation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in compliance with an approved payment plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred by an unsatisfied sentence` IF
        `sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor`
    AND (NOT (`completed the period of incarceration` AND `paid all fines, costs and restitution`))
    AND (NOT (    `paroled, or in compliance with all terms of probation`
              AND (`paid all fines, costs and restitution` OR `in compliance with an approved payment plan`)))

-- s 432(10): "Assistance shall not be granted to any applicant or recipient who is under eighteen years of age and who has
-- never been married and is pregnant and/or caring for a dependent child unless the minor parent is residing with a
-- parent, legal guardian or other adult relative or in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement approved by the
-- department." "Exceptions ... will be granted by the department if it is determined that an exception would best serve
-- the health and safety of the minor parent and the child or if the minor parent can present evidence that the parent,
-- legal guardian or other adult" refuses or cannot house them, poses a threat, has abused, has neglected, or "has spent
-- the minor parent's assistance in an improper manner" ((i)-(v)). The department's determination is a judgment: a fact.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `has ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is pregnant or caring for a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lives with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative, or in an approved adult-supervised arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the department has determined an exception would best serve the health and safety of the minor parent and child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `can present evidence of one of the grounds in s 432(10)(i) to (v)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred as a minor parent` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 18
    AND (NOT `has ever been married`)
    AND `is pregnant or caring for a dependent child`
    AND (NOT `lives with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative, or in an approved adult-supervised arrangement`)
    AND (NOT (   `the department has determined an exception would best serve the health and safety of the minor parent and child`
              OR `can present evidence of one of the grounds in s 432(10)(i) to (v)`))

DECLARE `Person's circumstances` HAS
    `is a citizen of the United States`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `federal law specifically requires assistance to this non-citizen`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a resident of Pennsylvania`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an inmate of a public institution`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `disposed of property worth $500 or more without fair consideration within two years before applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `eligible for State supplemental assistance`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred by an unsatisfied sentence`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred as a minor parent`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- The first bar that applies, in the order above, or NOTHING. Each bar alone defeats assistance.
GIVEN p IS A `Person's circumstances`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Bar to assistance`
`the bar to assistance` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (p's `is a citizen of the United States`)) AND (NOT (p's `federal law specifically requires assistance to this non-citizen`))
            THEN JUST `not a citizen, and federal law does not specifically require assistance (s 432.22)`
        IF NOT (p's `is a resident of Pennsylvania`)
            THEN JUST `not a resident of Pennsylvania (s 432(5)(i)); a transient may be given up to seven days of assistance as vendor payments`
        IF p's `is an inmate of a public institution`
            THEN JUST `an inmate of a public institution (s 432(4)(ii))`
        IF p's `disposed of property worth $500 or more without fair consideration within two years before applying` AND (NOT (p's `eligible for State supplemental assistance`))
            THEN JUST `disposed of property worth $500 or more without fair consideration in the two years before applying, and not eligible for State supplemental assistance (s 432(4)(i))`
        IF p's `barred by an unsatisfied sentence`
            THEN JUST `sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor and has not satisfied the penalty (s 432(9))`
        IF p's `barred as a minor parent`
            THEN JUST `an unmarried parent under 18 who is not living with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative or in an approved adult-supervised arrangement, and no exception applies (s 432(10))`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 432(6): "Aid to families with dependent children shall not be paid to any family for any month in which any
-- caretaker relative with whom the child is living is, on the last day of such month, participating in a strike".
GIVEN `a caretaker relative is participating in a strike on the last day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no aid is paid to the family for the month because of a strike` IF
    `a caretaker relative is participating in a strike on the last day of the month`

§§ `s 432.5 -- resources`

-- s 432.5(b): the home is retained "without reference to its value". (c): "Other property in excess of two hundred fifty
-- dollars ($250) for a single person ... and other property in excess of one thousand dollars ($1,000) for assistance
-- groups with more than one person shall be considered an available resource." Not counted: (1) rings, heirlooms,
-- clothing, toys; (2) household furnishings and personal effects; (3) employment, rehabilitation or self-care equipment;
-- (4) "One motor vehicle per assistance group ... When the difference between the fair market value ... and the amount
-- owed on the purchase price of the vehicle is less than forty thousand dollars ($40,000)"; (5) retroactive assistance from
-- a prehearing conference or fair hearing decision.
-- `other property` is the value of everything not in (b) or (c)(1)-(5) and not the excluded vehicle: cash, bank accounts,
-- other vehicles, non-home real property (s 432.5(d)) and the like (a fact). A vehicle whose equity is $40,000 or more is
-- not excluded and is counted at that equity (the Code gives no other value; NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `number of persons in the assistance group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the property allowance` `number of persons in the assistance group` MEANS
    IF `number of persons in the assistance group` GREATER THAN 1 THEN 1000 ELSE 250

GIVEN `number of persons in the assistance group` IS A NUMBER
      `other property` IS A NUMBER
      `equity in the one vehicle` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the available resource` `number of persons in the assistance group` `other property` `equity in the one vehicle` MEANS
    LET `vehicle counted` MEANS IF `equity in the one vehicle` LESS THAN 40000 THEN 0 ELSE `equity in the one vehicle`
        `counted` MEANS `other property` PLUS `vehicle counted`
        `allowance` MEANS `the property allowance` `number of persons in the assistance group`
    IN IF `counted` GREATER THAN `allowance` THEN `counted` MINUS `allowance` ELSE 0

§§ `s 432.12(a) -- whose income counts, and the earned income disregard`

-- s 432.12(a): "In determining need for aid to families with dependent children, the gross income of all members of the
-- assistance group who are fourteen years of age or older shall be considered except the gross income of a member of the
-- assistance group who is between the ages of fourteen and twenty-one, is a full or part-time student, and is not employed
-- full time or income which is specifically excluded by Federal or State law." "Between the ages of fourteen and
-- twenty-one" is read as 14 to 21 inclusive (NOTES.md finding 7).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `is a full or part-time student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is employed full time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member's gross income is considered` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 14
    AND (NOT (    `age` AT MOST 21
              AND `is a full or part-time student`
              AND (NOT `is employed full time`)))

-- "Fifty percent of gross earned income shall be disregarded when determining eligibility for recipients." The disregard
-- is stated for recipients only, not applicants (NOTES.md finding 8). Income "specifically excluded by Federal or State
-- law" is left out of the inputs.
GIVEN `is a recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gross earned income considered` IS A NUMBER
      `gross unearned income considered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income counted for eligibility` `is a recipient` `gross earned income considered` `gross unearned income considered` MEANS
    IF `is a recipient`
    THEN (`gross earned income considered` TIMES 50%) PLUS `gross unearned income considered`
    ELSE `gross earned income considered` PLUS `gross unearned income considered`

§§ `s 432(5)(ii) -- a family resident less than twelve months`

-- s 432(5)(ii): "Cash assistance for applicants and recipients of aid to families with dependent children who have resided
-- in this Commonwealth for less than twelve months shall not exceed the lesser of the maximum assistance payment that would
-- have been received from the applicant's or recipient's state of prior residence or the maximum assistance payment
-- available to the applicant or recipient in this Commonwealth." Both maximums are facts.
GIVEN `months resident in Pennsylvania` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum payment in the state of prior residence` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum payment in Pennsylvania` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most cash assistance can be` `months resident in Pennsylvania` `the maximum payment in the state of prior residence` `the maximum payment in Pennsylvania` MEANS
    IF `months resident in Pennsylvania` LESS THAN 12
       AND `the maximum payment in the state of prior residence` LESS THAN `the maximum payment in Pennsylvania`
    THEN `the maximum payment in the state of prior residence`
    ELSE `the maximum payment in Pennsylvania`

§§ `s 405.1 -- RESET work requirements`

-- s 405.1(a.3): "An applicant or recipient may be exempt from the requirements of subsection (a.2) if any of the following
-- apply: (1) ... a verified physical or mental disability which temporarily or permanently precludes the applicant or
-- recipient from any form of employment or work-related activity ... (2) ... a specified relative caring for a child who is
-- under six years of age and for whom alternate child care arrangements are unavailable. (3) ... under eighteen years of
-- age." The disability must be "assessed by a physician or psychologist" and verified in writing (a fact).
GIVEN `has a verified disability precluding any employment or work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a specified relative caring for a child under six with no alternate child care available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be exempt from the work requirements` IF
        `has a verified disability precluding any employment or work-related activity`
    OR  `is a specified relative caring for a child under six with no alternate child care available`
    OR  `age` LESS THAN 18

DECLARE `Work requirement` IS ONE OF
    `exempt under s 405.1(a.3); may still take part (s 405.1(b)); one under 18 must pursue a high school diploma or equivalency`
    `must seek employment, accept any offer of employment and maintain employment (s 405.1(a.2)(1))`
    `must also take part in a work-related activity, beginning with an independent job search of up to eight weeks (s 405.1(a.2)(2), (3))`
    `having received assistance for 24 months, must work or take part in subsidized employment, work experience, on-the-job training, community service or workfare for an average of at least 20 hours a week (s 405.1(a.2)(6))`

-- s 405.1(a.2)(1): every nonexempt individual "shall seek employment, accept any offer of employment and maintain
-- employment". (2): one "who is not employed for an average of at least twenty hours per week shall be required to
-- participate in a work-related activity". (3): the initial activity is "an independent job search for a period not to
-- exceed eight weeks". (6): "A recipient who has received assistance for twenty-four months, whether those months are
-- consecutive or interrupted, must work ... for an average of at least twenty hours per week."
GIVEN `exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `average hours employed per week` IS A NUMBER
      `months of assistance received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Work requirement`
`the work requirement that applies` `exempt` `average hours employed per week` `months of assistance received` MEANS
    IF `exempt`
    THEN `exempt under s 405.1(a.3); may still take part (s 405.1(b)); one under 18 must pursue a high school diploma or equivalency`
    ELSE IF `months of assistance received` AT LEAST 24
         THEN `having received assistance for 24 months, must work or take part in subsidized employment, work experience, on-the-job training, community service or workfare for an average of at least 20 hours a week (s 405.1(a.2)(6))`
         ELSE IF `average hours employed per week` AT LEAST 20
              THEN `must seek employment, accept any offer of employment and maintain employment (s 405.1(a.2)(1))`
              ELSE `must also take part in a work-related activity, beginning with an independent job search of up to eight weeks (s 405.1(a.2)(2), (3))`

§§ `s 432.3 -- disqualification for failing the work requirements`

-- s 432.3(a): a nonexempt applicant or recipient who "without good cause" quits or cuts earnings, fails to apply for work,
-- or refuses a work-related activity or a bona fide job "shall be disqualified from receiving assistance as follows:
-- (1) A minimum of thirty days for the first violation and continuing thereafter until such time as he or she is willing to
-- comply ...; a minimum of sixty days for the second violation and continuing thereafter until ...; and permanently for a
-- third violation. (2) If the reason for the disqualification occurs during the first twenty-four months that cash
-- assistance is received ... only the individual is disqualified. If ... after the individual has received assistance for
-- more than twenty-four months ... the disqualification is imposed on the entire assistance group."
-- Good cause is the department's finding (a fact). A violation in month 24 itself falls in "the first twenty-four
-- months" (NOTES.md finding 10).
DECLARE `Disqualification length` IS ONE OF
    `at least 30 days, and until willing to comply`
    `at least 60 days, and until willing to comply`
    `permanent`

DECLARE `Who is disqualified` IS ONE OF
    `only the individual`
    `the entire assistance group`

DECLARE `Disqualification outcome` HAS
    `length` IS A `Disqualification length`
    `who`    IS A `Who is disqualified`

GIVEN `which violation this is` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disqualification length`
`the disqualification length` `which violation this is` MEANS
    IF `which violation this is` AT MOST 1
    THEN `at least 30 days, and until willing to comply`
    ELSE IF `which violation this is` EQUALS 2
         THEN `at least 60 days, and until willing to comply`
         ELSE `permanent`

GIVEN `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Who is disqualified`
`who is disqualified` `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred` MEANS
    IF `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred` AT MOST 24
    THEN `only the individual`
    ELSE `the entire assistance group`

GIVEN `which violation this is` IS A NUMBER
      `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disqualification outcome`
`the disqualification` `which violation this is` `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred` MEANS
    `Disqualification outcome` WITH
        `length` IS `the disqualification length` `which violation this is`
        `who`    IS `who is disqualified` `months of cash assistance received when the reason occurred`

-- The earliest day a disqualification of at least N days can end (the person counts days from the day it begins).
GIVEN `the day it begins` IS A DATE
      `which violation this is` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest day a disqualification can end` `the day it begins` `which violation this is` MEANS
    IF `which violation this is` AT MOST 1
    THEN JUST (`the day it begins` PLUS 30)
    ELSE IF `which violation this is` EQUALS 2
         THEN JUST (`the day it begins` PLUS 60)
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 405.1(a.4), 432.14, 432.17, 423 -- duties with a deadline (regulative)`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant or recipient`
    `the department`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `comply with the employment and work-related activity requirements`
    `report the change in circumstances`
    `request a fair hearing`

-- s 405.1(a.4)(1): for one exempt because of a disability, "(i) If the condition ceases during the first twenty-two months
-- that the recipient receives cash assistance ... the recipient shall be required to comply with subsection (a.2)
-- immediately. (ii) If the condition ceases after the recipient has received cash assistance for twenty-two months or more
-- ... within eight weeks." Days are counted from the day the condition ceases; failing to comply leads to s 432.3.
GIVEN `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days to comply after a disability exemption ends` `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased` MEANS
    IF `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased` AT LEAST 22 THEN 56 ELSE 0

GIVEN `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to comply once a disability exemption ends` `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MUST  `comply with the employment and work-related activity requirements`
    WITHIN (`days to comply after a disability exemption ends` `months of cash assistance when the condition ceased`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant or recipient` BECAUSE "the work requirements were not met once the disability exemption ended (s 405.1(a.4)(1)); disqualification under s 432.3 follows unless there is good cause"

-- s 432.14(b): "Each applicant for or recipient or payee of such assistance shall be responsible for reporting accurately
-- and within a reasonable specified period those facts required of him pursuant to the explanation provided by the
-- department." The period is the department's (a fact, in days from the change).
GIVEN `the reporting period the department specified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to report a change` `the reporting period the department specified` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MUST  `report the change in circumstances`
    WITHIN `the reporting period the department specified`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant or recipient` BECAUSE "a change the department explained must be reported was not reported within the period it specified (s 432.14(b)); an overpayment may be recouped under s 432.16"

-- s 432.17: "The department shall provide timely and adequate notice in all cases of intended action to discontinue,
-- terminate, suspend or reduce an assistance grant" (except where adequate notice alone is consistent with federal law).
-- "'Timely notice' means notice which is mailed ten days before the intended change would be effective."
GIVEN `the day the notice is mailed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the change can take effect` `the day the notice is mailed` MEANS
    `the day the notice is mailed` PLUS 10

-- s 423(a): "If the appellant is already receiving assistance and requests a fair hearing within the timely notice period,
-- assistance shall not be terminated until a decision is rendered in the hearing except in those appeals where the sole
-- issue is one of State or Federal law or policy or change in State or Federal law or policy." The appeal is a right
-- (a "may"); requesting within the period keeps assistance going.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to request a fair hearing within the timely notice period` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient`
    MAY   `request a fair hearing`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED

GIVEN `already receiving assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requested a fair hearing within the timely notice period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sole issue is State or Federal law or policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `assistance continues until the hearing decision` IF
        `already receiving assistance`
    AND `requested a fair hearing within the timely notice period`
    AND (NOT `the sole issue is State or Federal law or policy`)
